00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:04.019
Nicole: So why is cyber
security testing so important?

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:07.890
Abraham: Cyber security testing
helps to identify weaknesses or

00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:11.210
vulnerabilities before they are
found by malicious threat actors.

00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:15.629
Nicole: By simulating the behaviour
of threat actors, cyber security

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:20.290
experts can help to identify any
issues with a system and how these

00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:22.290
might potentially be exploited.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:27.309
Companies often do security testing
after installing new systems, apps

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:31.869
and infrastructure to make sure that
every aspect of their system is secure.

00:00:32.530 --> 00:00:36.459
By identifying these, at the time
of installation, weaknesses or

00:00:36.490 --> 00:00:40.580
vulnerabilities can be assessed and
organisations can prioritise and

00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:42.930
handle any risks more effectively.

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:46.980
Abraham: Different types of testing
can show up different weaknesses.

00:00:47.090 --> 00:00:51.689
For example, social engineering testing
can highlight issues with procedures

00:00:52.019 --> 00:00:56.640
and identify how susceptible staff
might be to social engineering attacks.

00:00:56.690 --> 00:01:00.120
This can then be used can be used to
develop training to raise staff awareness.

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:04.269
Nicole: Pen testing can help personnel
learn how to handle a malicious

00:01:04.269 --> 00:01:06.250
attack if it happens for real.

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:12.019
Red teaming or ethical hacking can be used
to systematically identify an attack path

00:01:12.350 --> 00:01:17.640
looking for all the unnoticeable gaps such
as backdoors, open windows, and other ways

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:19.800
of breaching an organisation’s system.

00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:25.089
Abraham: Cyber security testing can
be costly, but it can save more money

00:01:25.099 --> 00:01:29.039
in the long term as it can protect
against expensive cyber-attacks that

00:01:29.039 --> 00:01:33.039
could impact an organisation in the
way it functions and its reputation.

00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:37.830
Nicole: Think of the costs involved in
an expensive ransomware attack, losing

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:44.320
data to competitors, replacing software
and hardware or even data, and any fines

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:46.630
that go along with it for breaching GDPR.

00:01:47.299 --> 00:01:50.260
Abraham: Imagine how costly it could
be for an organisation to suffer

00:01:50.260 --> 00:01:54.440
significant downtime especially if
they have to close down the system

00:01:54.470 --> 00:01:55.960
and go offline to fix the problem.

00:01:56.170 --> 00:01:59.369
Nicole: Some standards require
organisations to perform regular

00:01:59.370 --> 00:02:02.799
penetration or other types of
security testing to meet industry

00:02:02.799 --> 00:02:04.460
standards and regulations.

00:02:04.910 --> 00:02:11.040
Such as ISO 27001 the standard
for information security and GDPR

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:14.859
where organisations that process
Personal information and data,

00:02:15.170 --> 00:02:18.079
have to make sure that they have
appropriate security measures in

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:20.560
place to identify vulnerabilities.

00:02:21.230 --> 00:02:27.190
The PCI DSS Payment card industry data
security standard requires vulnerability

00:02:27.190 --> 00:02:29.049
scanning as part of its standard.

00:02:29.890 --> 00:02:34.090
Abraham: Security testing and evaluating
testing is a proactive approach that

00:02:34.099 --> 00:02:39.320
helps to identify the potential security
risks and help to show how to fix issues.

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:43.540
It helps to reduce threats and risks
in systems to minimize the chance of

00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:47.589
loss resulting from a cybersecurity
breach and taking data protection

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:52.489
seriously, by regular testing, helps
organisations to cement a relationship

00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:54.079
of trust with their customers.

